WEBVTT

00:01.850 --> 00:07.530
Master, help me... Help me...

00:07.530 --> 00:12.350
Master, I miss you... Help me...

00:45.390 --> 00:53.690
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

02:04.310 --> 02:09.690
<b>Episode 11 "Belgrieve's Decision"</b>

02:08.800 --> 02:10.420
What are you doing?

02:10.420 --> 02:12.110
You can't even dodge that?

02:12.860 --> 02:14.120
Shut up!

02:17.610 --> 02:20.570
Hey, that's the demon king's power.

02:26.120 --> 02:28.570
Don't go relying on that.

02:28.570 --> 02:30.790
Use too much and it'll consume you.

02:30.790 --> 02:31.850
Damn it...

02:38.730 --> 02:43.730
That's better. Focus on your 
body's mana-generating organ.

02:43.730 --> 02:46.650
Separate your mana from the demon king's.

02:47.980 --> 02:49.040
Granny...

02:49.040 --> 02:50.720
Byaku, are you okay?

02:51.030 --> 02:54.470
Come at me again, you old hag. 
I've got the hang of it now.

02:54.470 --> 02:58.270
What? How dare you call
 a spring chicken a hag?!

03:03.870 --> 03:10.240
We'll have to fix that cheeky mouth of 
yours before we address your mana.

03:05.260 --> 03:07.740
Are you scared to fight?

03:07.740 --> 03:08.750
Yes.

03:09.500 --> 03:15.230
I felt like I could do anything 
when I was using Solomon's power,

03:13.050 --> 03:19.580
Go on, say it. "Please, miss, would 
you do me the favor of another round?"

03:15.230 --> 03:18.360
but now I'm powerless.

03:19.580 --> 03:22.500
Shut up, hag!

03:22.510 --> 03:25.640
But there's no telling what may happen.

03:22.810 --> 03:24.170
You fool!

03:25.400 --> 03:27.540
I told you not to use that mana!

03:25.640 --> 03:28.320
You should learn to use magic, too.

03:27.540 --> 03:29.830
Don't let your emotions control you, brat.

03:29.540 --> 03:31.400
From Granny Maria?

03:31.380 --> 03:32.520
Damn it!

03:32.090 --> 03:34.680
Well, maybe we can find someone nicer.

03:32.860 --> 03:34.090
Weak!

03:40.800 --> 03:42.820
We're going back to Turnera.

03:42.820 --> 03:45.070
Just you wait, cowberries!

03:45.590 --> 03:47.790
You're a weirdo.

03:47.790 --> 03:49.730
Quiet, Byaku.

03:49.730 --> 03:53.290
What's better than having a home to return to?

03:53.940 --> 03:55.760
You're dumb enough already,

03:55.760 --> 03:58.630
but you get even dumber 
when it comes to your dad.

03:58.630 --> 04:01.950
Ange's love for Mr. Bel is powerful indeed.

04:02.920 --> 04:06.470
Your dad's that old redhead, right?

04:06.470 --> 04:07.710
What's so great about him?

04:09.720 --> 04:11.080
Byaku...

04:11.740 --> 04:14.860
You'll understand once you meet him.

04:15.220 --> 04:19.090
That's right. I know you've heard
all her stories about him.

04:19.460 --> 04:22.370
And his hands are so warm!

04:22.370 --> 04:24.980
You only met him for a second.

04:24.980 --> 04:27.610
Well, he saved me.

04:27.990 --> 04:30.450
Yeah, after you attacked him.

04:28.060 --> 04:31.860
<i>There are fewer occasions to fight in Turnera.</i>

04:30.920 --> 04:31.860
Byaku!

04:31.860 --> 04:36.610
<i>Byaku won't have to use mana 
he hasn't mastered yet.</i>

04:32.230 --> 04:35.210
Anyway, you've gotten too soft recently.

04:35.770 --> 04:39.880
But warm hands are a sign of kindness!

04:36.910 --> 04:41.710
<i>And Char will be safer there, too.</i>

04:39.880 --> 04:42.050
You just don't get it.

04:42.050 --> 04:47.380
And I'll get plenty of time with 
my dad. It's the perfect plan.

04:48.240 --> 04:49.850
I'm so smart, it's scary.

04:49.850 --> 04:50.770
Hey, Anessa.

04:51.380 --> 04:52.510
What is it, Byaku?

04:52.750 --> 04:55.160
Do you want to go see her dad, too?

04:55.160 --> 05:01.020
Well, I'll say being around 
Mr. Bel makes me feel safe.

05:06.020 --> 05:09.040
I've delivered your letter.

05:09.400 --> 05:14.530
Don't think you can trick us.

05:16.680 --> 05:20.540
This is awful... What terrible timing.

05:20.980 --> 05:25.840
You can no longer pretend 
to be ignorant, Lionel.

05:25.840 --> 05:28.310
Hasn't Ms. Ange already left?

05:28.890 --> 05:32.210
If only this had come sooner...

05:40.030 --> 05:42.990
It rarely rains this time 
of year in the north.

05:42.990 --> 05:45.320
I hope nothing bad happens.

05:45.320 --> 05:50.310
Come now, Graham. Don't jinx us.

05:50.310 --> 05:52.960
You make it sound like something really will.

05:53.800 --> 05:56.440
Forgive me, Bel. Bad habit.

05:56.960 --> 05:58.800
Gramps in trouble?

05:59.780 --> 06:01.290
I'm no match for Bel.

06:01.290 --> 06:02.790
Hey! Food's ready!

06:05.580 --> 06:09.780
It'll be difficult to leave Turnera 
once winter arrives, right?

06:10.170 --> 06:13.670
Yeah. We get a lot of snow here,

06:14.050 --> 06:16.590
though I doubt as much as the elven lands.

06:16.590 --> 06:18.430
It'll still be tough to leave.

06:19.500 --> 06:21.200
I see.

06:21.200 --> 06:25.200
I'm thinking setting out before then.

06:26.430 --> 06:28.940
Where will you go?

06:29.180 --> 06:32.460
South. Turnera is nice,

06:32.460 --> 06:36.100
but I still want to become 
and adventurer like you.

06:36.100 --> 06:38.210
I want to see all sorts of places.

06:38.210 --> 06:40.600
I doubt I can stop you.

06:40.600 --> 06:42.500
Mary leaving?

06:42.500 --> 06:45.560
Yeah, but not forever.

06:45.560 --> 06:49.320
I swear I'll become a first-rate 
adventurer and come back here.

06:49.660 --> 06:51.220
To tell you the truth...

06:51.540 --> 06:55.290
I've been thinking about leaving town myself.

06:55.290 --> 06:56.530
You, too?

06:57.230 --> 07:00.860
I still have a few more people 
I'd like to face.

07:02.590 --> 07:04.810
Well, no helping that.

07:04.810 --> 07:07.070
But what about Hannah?

07:07.070 --> 07:09.030
We've already discussed it.

07:09.030 --> 07:11.870
This will be my last tour.

07:12.410 --> 07:15.370
Then you'll be returning as well?

07:15.650 --> 07:17.750
Don't keep us waiting too long.

07:18.560 --> 07:20.580
I won't.

07:20.860 --> 07:24.340
What's all this?
I underestimated you, Duncan.

07:24.340 --> 07:26.580
So, know when you're heading out?

07:26.920 --> 07:29.630
Yeah, after the fall festival.

07:29.630 --> 07:31.870
Then you're staying longer than me.

07:31.870 --> 07:35.090
Mary, you should stay for the festival, too.

07:35.090 --> 07:37.090
What? Why?

07:37.390 --> 07:40.450
Lots of caravans and merchants will be coming.

07:40.450 --> 07:43.100
You can leave with them.

07:43.490 --> 07:46.070
What? No way! That sounds lame.

07:46.070 --> 07:48.350
Besides, traveling alone is easier.

07:49.810 --> 07:51.980
Planning to get lost again?

07:51.980 --> 07:57.380
Lady Mary, adventurers should 
always minimize costs and risks.

07:57.690 --> 07:59.360
Duncan is right.

08:01.030 --> 08:02.880
I'll do what I can.

08:02.880 --> 08:04.810
Mary upset?

08:06.320 --> 08:07.830
Don't laugh!

08:07.830 --> 08:12.180
<i>I've gotten used to how 
lively things are here now.</i>

08:10.850 --> 08:13.770
I've given this a lot of thought, okay?

08:12.620 --> 08:15.640
<i>I'll miss them both when they're gone.</i>

08:21.760 --> 08:23.530
Say that again!

08:23.530 --> 08:29.180
Y-You see, Ms. Ange, this is coming 
from Grand Duke Estogal, not us.

08:29.180 --> 08:30.560
Don't be ridiculous!

08:30.560 --> 08:33.100
I don't care if he's a grand duke.

08:33.100 --> 08:36.240
He has no right to order me anywhere!

08:36.240 --> 08:38.940
Ange, calm down.

08:39.440 --> 08:42.130
This is not Lionel's fault.

08:42.390 --> 08:45.640
If I go to Estogal now,
 it'll be winter before you know it.

08:45.640 --> 08:48.350
Then I won't be able to 
make it back to Turnera.

08:48.350 --> 08:50.410
In any case, I'm not going.

08:50.410 --> 08:52.790
I don't care about balls or honors.

08:52.790 --> 08:55.020
I'm begging you, Ms. Ange!

08:55.020 --> 08:59.420
We're screwed if we end up on 
Grand Duke Estogal's bad side!

08:59.710 --> 09:03.700
Whatever. I'm sure they'll be 
satisfied giving you the axe.

09:03.700 --> 09:06.200
They will <i>literally</i>, you hear me?

09:06.200 --> 09:08.800
I don't want to die yet!

09:09.430 --> 09:13.560
Uncle Silver and General Muscles, 
are you on his side?

09:13.830 --> 09:19.200
That letter was addressed to the guild 
with instructions to send you to Estogal.

09:19.200 --> 09:23.580
This isn't just your problem anymore, Ange.

09:25.090 --> 09:28.640
Oh, come on! I can't believe the two of you.

09:28.640 --> 09:31.830
We should reject their damn request.

09:32.930 --> 09:34.080
Mr. Cheborg?

09:34.400 --> 09:38.950
If they come bother us, 
we can just crush 'em then.

09:39.430 --> 09:41.840
Who cares if he's a grand duke?

09:41.840 --> 09:45.340
A buncha wimps working together can't beat us.

09:45.600 --> 09:48.850
We can't do that! Right, Mr. Dortos?!

09:49.190 --> 09:52.710
Actually, with the right perspective,
 it's an option.

09:52.710 --> 09:56.350
You've got me and Cheborg. 
If we could convince Maria to join us...

09:56.350 --> 10:00.360
Absolutely not! Do you want to turn 
Orphen into a war zone?

10:00.360 --> 10:03.690
Besides, Mr. Cheborg, isn't the 
duke's place your old stomping ground?!

10:07.370 --> 10:09.600
I should just go, right?

10:10.810 --> 10:12.500
M-Ms. Ange?

10:13.460 --> 10:19.500
Fighting a duke's army sounds fun, 
but Dad would get angry at me.

10:23.530 --> 10:27.230
Goodness gracious.
She's finally grown up, hasn't she?

10:27.630 --> 10:31.920
Without a doubt. It's bittersweet.

10:32.390 --> 10:35.790
Anyway, I don't like what 
Grand Duke Estogal is doing.

10:35.790 --> 10:38.070
Now <i>that</i> I agree with.

10:38.070 --> 10:43.410
I sense a political motive behind honoring 
her now for defeating that demon king.

10:44.000 --> 10:47.290
Still, I'm glad Ms. Ange has calmed down.

10:47.940 --> 10:51.790
I'm sorry for making you two play my stooges.

10:55.640 --> 11:00.760
Wait... wasn't that all an act 
to make her change her mind?

11:01.380 --> 11:03.840
Come on, say something!

11:03.840 --> 11:05.870
Why won't you look at me?!

11:11.760 --> 11:14.360
Wh-What's wrong, Sister?

11:14.360 --> 11:16.190
I don't know what to do.

11:16.630 --> 11:18.110
What's got you upset?

11:18.370 --> 11:20.410
Our trip to Turnera's postponed.

11:21.380 --> 11:22.390
Wh-Why?

11:31.360 --> 11:32.660
I see.

11:32.660 --> 11:34.330
So that's why you're here.

11:34.330 --> 11:37.450
Seriously?! This noble's just being selfish!

11:37.450 --> 11:40.410
You defeated that demon king a year ago,

11:40.410 --> 11:42.590
and he wants to honor you <i>now?</i>

11:42.590 --> 11:44.170
Right, Ane?

11:44.170 --> 11:48.940
Yeah, but you can't stand up a grand duke.

11:48.940 --> 11:53.680
So Dad and the cowberries will have to wait.

11:54.600 --> 11:56.940
But I wanted to see Mr. Bel...

11:57.590 --> 12:00.440
So, what are your plans for now?

12:00.440 --> 12:05.000
It takes two weeks to reach
 Estogal CIty by carriage.

12:05.000 --> 12:07.450
So a whole month to get there and back.

12:07.760 --> 12:11.000
You won't be leaving as soon
 as you get there, you know?

12:11.000 --> 12:13.610
They'll keep you for several days, at least.

12:13.610 --> 12:17.450
I know. That's why I wanted 
to ask you about these two.

12:17.760 --> 12:23.460
I thought maybe I could take them
 if you guys came, too.

12:23.460 --> 12:27.970
I get it. You'll be super busy over there.

12:28.250 --> 12:32.430
Yeah, and I can't protect them alone.

12:32.430 --> 12:35.450
I let Ms. Rosetta get hurt the other day.

12:35.730 --> 12:41.060
Then aren't they better off
 staying here with us?

12:41.600 --> 12:44.870
Only if you wouldn't miss us, that is.

12:44.870 --> 12:48.450
Of course not. Who do you take me for?

12:48.450 --> 12:55.240
I know! Why don't Ane and 
I take Char and Byaku to Turnera?

12:55.240 --> 12:59.280
Then all our prep won't go to waste,
 and we'll get to see Mr. Bel!

13:02.450 --> 13:05.530
Don't go without me!

13:05.530 --> 13:06.920
No! Don't do it!

13:07.860 --> 13:10.380
Sorry, sorry! I was only kidding!

13:10.380 --> 13:13.360
We obviously wouldn't go 
to Turnera without you.

13:13.360 --> 13:15.170
There, there. That's a good girl.

13:15.170 --> 13:16.920
No!

13:16.120 --> 13:17.680
Sister...

13:17.680 --> 13:20.190
Miri, how could you?

13:20.190 --> 13:25.270
I-I'm sorry, okay? I didn't think she'd cry!

13:27.910 --> 13:32.400
Well then, you're all staying here in 
Orphen while I head out solo.

13:32.400 --> 13:34.120
That's the best choice.

13:34.120 --> 13:37.420
Without constraints, 
you can leave as soon as you're done.

13:37.420 --> 13:41.440
Thanks. I appreciate all of this,
 you two. Also...

13:41.910 --> 13:45.610
Don't even <i>think</i> about 
sneaking off to Turnera.

13:45.610 --> 13:47.160
Got it, Miri?

13:48.060 --> 13:50.940
I said I was joking.

13:51.450 --> 13:53.670
Are you two okay with that, too?

13:53.670 --> 13:55.150
Y-Yes!

13:55.150 --> 14:00.150
Then you'll be staying with us. 
Sorry the place is a mess.

14:00.520 --> 14:03.390
I-I'll help you clean, Ane.

14:03.820 --> 14:05.240
Thanks.

14:05.240 --> 14:07.890
So, when do you depart, Ange?

14:08.220 --> 14:11.720
Tomorrow. I'm already packed anyway.

14:11.720 --> 14:15.470
Okay. The sun's long set, 
so let's hit to our usual spot.

14:15.470 --> 14:17.400
We're gonna eat tonight!

14:18.160 --> 14:19.400
Your treat, Miri?

14:20.860 --> 14:22.920
S-So be it.

14:30.500 --> 14:32.180
That's enough for now.

14:32.470 --> 14:35.970
Sure. Thanks for helping me, Graham.

14:39.620 --> 14:43.280
<i>This isn't good. I can't focus.</i>

14:46.750 --> 14:49.600
<i>Why am I dreaming about that now?</i>

14:50.670 --> 14:52.280
All right!

14:52.280 --> 14:53.980
I landed a hit!

14:53.980 --> 14:55.770
Did you see that, Granduncle?!

14:55.770 --> 14:57.780
I did. Nicely done.

14:58.010 --> 14:59.620
I know when I'm beaten.

14:59.620 --> 15:02.290
You've gotten stronger, Lady Mary.

15:04.610 --> 15:06.280
I'm impressed, Mary.

15:06.580 --> 15:09.380
Now I won't have to worry 
about you leaving Turnera.

15:17.610 --> 15:18.890
We have a winner.

15:19.110 --> 15:21.040
Congratulations, Miss Elf.

15:21.890 --> 15:24.690
Is this for me? Thanks.

15:25.260 --> 15:27.010
How's it look, Mit?

15:27.700 --> 15:29.310
Good?

15:30.070 --> 15:32.590
He gave that meat to me, you know.

15:32.590 --> 15:33.620
Is it tasty?

15:33.620 --> 15:34.840
Tasty.

15:34.840 --> 15:36.050
Hey, Mary.

15:39.520 --> 15:43.470
This is the swordsman I told 
you about. She's skilled.

15:43.470 --> 15:45.350
Mary, this is—

15:45.350 --> 15:46.600
A-An elf?!

15:46.870 --> 15:48.590
Huh? Who are you?

15:48.590 --> 15:53.280
Mary, I called you over to 
introduce you. Don't act like that.

15:53.640 --> 15:55.830
She's a traveling merchant.

15:55.830 --> 16:00.090
Didn't I tell you we'd find someone 
to give you a ride to Orphen?

16:00.090 --> 16:05.370
That mean you're traveling south? 
You got a carriage?

16:05.370 --> 16:08.230
What? Yes, I do. Um...

16:08.230 --> 16:12.590
She's not the most refined, 
but she's not a bad girl.

16:12.980 --> 16:18.230
I promise you'll be safer with her than 
a handful of average adventurers.

16:18.230 --> 16:21.410
Y-Yeah? Very well.

16:21.410 --> 16:24.250
I'm departing in two days. Is that all right?

16:24.980 --> 16:27.310
All right! Thanks a ton.

16:27.310 --> 16:30.260
The name's Marguerite. Nice to meet you.

16:30.900 --> 16:33.370
<i>Looks like they'll be fine.</i>

16:38.420 --> 16:41.350
You seem like you've got 
something on your mind.

16:41.350 --> 16:43.690
You can tell, huh?

16:44.140 --> 16:46.810
Tell me about it, my friend.

16:47.150 --> 16:48.290
Thanks.

16:48.990 --> 16:52.530
I just dreamt of the past
 for the first time in a while.

16:58.870 --> 17:00.570
Duncan, you look terrible!

17:01.660 --> 17:05.850
I see. Sounds like there's 
something for you to resolve.

17:06.140 --> 17:10.690
Your worries are stuck there like a thorn.

17:10.690 --> 17:15.490
You won't truly be able to 
move on unless you remove it.

17:15.490 --> 17:17.540
You're probably right.

17:18.330 --> 17:23.010
<i>I haven't overcome my past.
I just haven't faced it.</i>

17:23.350 --> 17:28.380
But Mary and Duncan are leaving.
 If I go, too...

17:28.950 --> 17:30.960
You're worried about Turnera?

17:31.500 --> 17:35.610
Yes. Something could still happen.

17:36.460 --> 17:38.610
Then I'll stay.

17:39.310 --> 17:41.280
In Turnera?

17:41.280 --> 17:43.740
I appreciate it, but are you sure?

17:43.740 --> 17:46.120
Weren't you going to keep traveling?

17:46.120 --> 17:51.620
I was originally pursuing Marguerite. 
She couldn't be trusted on her own.

17:51.940 --> 17:55.430
But now she should be fine without me.

17:55.430 --> 17:58.630
I see. Mary has certainly grown.

17:58.630 --> 18:03.630
Because of you, Bel. 
I'd like to repay the favor.

18:03.980 --> 18:07.020
Thank you, Graham. I appreciate it.

18:07.020 --> 18:09.850
I do have one request, however.

18:10.640 --> 18:15.930
While you're gone, can Mit stay with me?

18:16.770 --> 18:18.160
You'd be lonely?

18:19.100 --> 18:20.580
Lonely?

18:30.000 --> 18:31.880
Ms. Gil? What're you doing here?

18:31.880 --> 18:34.450
Turns out I was invited, too.

18:34.450 --> 18:35.900
What? Really?

18:36.530 --> 18:39.110
Just kidding. Lionel didn't tell you?

18:39.110 --> 18:40.940
No, he didn't...

18:41.460 --> 18:47.260
But he must been thinking of me
 to send a Triple A adventurer.

18:49.960 --> 18:52.760
I feel better having you with me!

18:52.760 --> 18:57.450
I'm honored. I hope I can live 
up to your expectations.

18:57.450 --> 19:00.040
Let's make it a good trip, Ange.

19:00.950 --> 19:01.910
Yeah!

19:02.360 --> 19:03.810
Stay strong!

19:03.810 --> 19:05.260
Go!

19:06.300 --> 19:07.270
Damn!

19:07.730 --> 19:10.030
Over there! It's coming from the side!

19:13.880 --> 19:14.920
When'd it get there?

19:15.290 --> 19:17.660
Hey, did you notice it sneaking up on us?

19:17.660 --> 19:20.660
Not at all! That guy is incredible.

19:21.470 --> 19:24.090
He's what our group is missing!

19:25.310 --> 19:28.610
I saw you just standing around again today!

19:28.610 --> 19:30.720
I was getting a read on the battle.

19:30.720 --> 19:33.650
Shut up! We don't tolerate 
useless adventurers!

19:33.650 --> 19:35.410
As of today, you're out!

19:39.760 --> 19:40.780
Hey.

19:41.340 --> 19:42.290
Who, me?

19:42.290 --> 19:44.360
Yeah. You're amazing.

19:44.360 --> 19:45.590
Amazing how?

19:45.590 --> 19:50.150
What do you mean? You noticed 
that sneak attack from our flank.

19:50.150 --> 19:52.120
Oh, I guess.

19:52.120 --> 19:53.490
I like you.

19:53.920 --> 19:56.510
Care to join our party?

19:58.010 --> 20:02.830
We'd love to have a lifesaver like you around.

20:10.530 --> 20:14.300
Will you come back?
 I know it would make them happy.

20:15.690 --> 20:18.610
I don't want to get in your way.

20:18.840 --> 20:21.520
I can't even serve as a decoy like this.

20:22.110 --> 20:27.940
You're all rank B now. 
You're nearly at the top.

20:27.940 --> 20:30.860
I wouldn't want to hold you back.

20:30.860 --> 20:33.380
But... But that's not...

20:33.380 --> 20:35.560
Don't make that face.

20:35.560 --> 20:38.970
All that matters is that
 we're alive and well.

20:38.970 --> 20:40.530
But we—

20:40.530 --> 20:41.530
I'm in a hurry.

20:42.130 --> 20:44.880
I have to deliver these herbs to the guild.

20:48.570 --> 20:52.900
Take care, Kasim. 
Say goodbye to the others for me.

20:54.070 --> 20:55.250
Bel!

21:00.760 --> 21:02.640
What a nasty dream.

21:03.790 --> 21:10.150
What should we have done for you, Bel?

21:26.330 --> 21:31.170
Once something's broken, there's no 
point in putting it back together.

21:34.820 --> 21:38.450
You again? You'll be in trouble
 if someone catches you.

21:38.450 --> 21:42.170
No one will come here. Everyone's so busy.

21:42.540 --> 21:45.940
They're bustling about the mansion 
getting ready for the ball.

21:45.940 --> 21:50.440
Then you should be with your betrothed.
 It's cold down here.

21:50.710 --> 21:52.670
A short visit won't hurt.

21:53.090 --> 21:56.130
Tell me more stories, Kasim.

21:57.300 --> 21:58.860
Fine.

21:59.760 --> 22:02.990
If you bring me another bottle.

23:34.970 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next Time</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.930
<b>"Confronting the Past"</b>
